  "title": "cpu_info: fix missing decl in else macro block",
  "description": "Wireshark builds are broken on Illumos systems (not sure where else this codepath is hit, probably more unusual platforms); likely none of the developers ever target a platform where this codegen path was taken, and so the code has unfortunately been broken for a while. `model_name` was used, but not declared within the scope.\n\nBug:\n```\n[  3%] Building C object wsutil/CMakeFiles/wsutil.dir/cpu_info.c.o\n/home/dsp/wireshark/wsutil/cpu_info.c: In function 'get_cpu_info':\n/home/dsp/wireshark/wsutil/cpu_info.c:415:5: error: 'model_name' undeclared (first use in this function); did you mean 'model_names'?\n  415 |     model_name = g_strdup(g_strstrip(CPUBrandString));\n      |     ^~~~~~~~~~\n      |     model_names\n/home/dsp/wireshark/wsutil/cpu_info.c:415:5: note: each undeclared identifier is reported only once for each function it appears in\n*** Error code 1\n```\n\nAfter changes:\n```\n[  3%] Building C object wsutil/CMakeFiles/wsutil.dir/cpu_info.c.o\n[  3%] Building C object wsutil/CMakeFiles/wsutil.dir/os_version_info.c.o\n```\n\nThe modification from `g_malloc` to `g_new` was performed automatically by the pre-commit hooks; I assume that the behaviour is correct, but someone might want to verify this. I'm not an expert here.",
